  "flags": [
    {"page": 36, "what": "The warband's minimum of 3 models is not imported: our templates hold no minimum."},
    {"page": 36, "what": "The PDF prints no equipment list of its own: \"All of the equipment lists from the rulebook apply\". The Skaven Hero and Skaven Henchmen lists are taken from our own Skaven warband, which is the rulebook's, not from any other PDF. \"Skaven Clan Mors may use the Skaven weapons as detailed in the rulebook\" is covered by those lists (Weeping Blades, Fighting Claws, Warplock Pistol, Blowpipe, Throwing Knives/Stars)."},
    {"page": 36, "what": "\"Skaven Heroes may use any of the Skaven Special Skills in the rulebook except for the Art of Silent Death\": our Skaven group holds the Art of Silent Death, so one new group, Skaven of Karak Azgal, holds our other four Skaven skills and serves both Karak Azgal Skaven warbands. See the decisions."},
    {"page": 38, "what": "The Rat Ogre is printed \"0.1\", read as 0-1."},
    {"page": 38, "what": "\"Note: Rat Ogres and Wolf Rats are alternative list entries to be confirmed\" is the author's note. Both are imported as printed."},
    {"page": 38, "what": "The Rat Ogre's Stupidity is not the shared rule (he is not stupid while a Skaven Hero is within 6\"), so it stays the Rat Ogres' own, as our other Skaven warbands' is."},
    {"page": 39, "what": "The Wolf Rats are M6 WS4 BS0 S4 T4 W1 I4 A2 Ld6 here, which is not the Clan Moulder Wolf Rat's profile. As printed; they take no race, as an animal."},
    {"page": 38, "what": "Henchmen are bought in groups of 1-5. No maximum is printed for Clanrats or Skavenslaves."},
    {"page": 36, "what": "Starting experience: Claw Leader 20, Mors Sorcerer and Stormvermin 8, Young Claws 0, Henchmen 0."}
  ]
